course: dictionary
lesson: 13429
title: Homeward
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Homeward means towards home. You can use it after a verb, as in «We walked homeward after the football match», or before a noun, as in «the homeward journey». The ending -ward shows direction, like upward or onward.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «We walked» tells you there was movement, and the rest of the sentence tells you where it was going. If you swap in «towards home» and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Homeward is a little formal. In everyday speech, people usually say «going home». In stories, characters often turn homeward at the end of an adventure, and in some stories a hero is «homeward bound».
fact: Homeward means towards home.
fact: Homewards means the same as homeward.
fact: «Homeward» can describe a verb, as in «We walked homeward», or a noun, as in «the homeward journey».
fact: In maths problems, the homeward journey is the trip back. If you go 12 km out and 12 km homeward, you travel 24 km in all.
fact: «Homeward bound» means heading back home, and it is often used in stories about long journeys.
exercise: «We walked homeward after the football match.» What does homeward mean? | *Towards home | Under the trees | Away from the match | Very fast
exercise: Which word in «the homeward bus was full of tired children» tells you the bus was going home? | *homeward | children | bus | tired
exercise: «We cycled 12 km out and 12 km homeward. How far did we cycle in all?» | 144 km | 12 km | 6 km | *24 km
test: «The sailors turned homeward as the sun went down.» What does homeward mean here? | Towards the shops | Towards the sea | Towards the sun | *Towards home
test: Odysseus is «homeward bound». What does that mean? | *Heading back home | Sailing to a new land | Lost at sea | Asleep in a boat
exam: Fill the gap with the best word: «The birds flew ___ at sunset.» | sideways | silently | underwater | *homeward
